# Greatest common divisor and least common multiple of two numbers.

π' → A
? → a
? → b
a → m
b → n

π' → B              # Euclid: (m, n) becomes (n, m mod n) until n is 0.
(1 ∩ n)·C + (1 ∸ n)·D → π

π' → C
m mod n → r
n → m
r → n
B → π

π' → D
m → ?               # the divisor
a:m·b → ?           # the multiple: a divided by the divisor, times b
Ω → π
